@operation("Eternal Justice")
  ┌─ OFFICIAL face · press_release · PUBLIC ─────────────────────
  │   equal before the law — one jurisdiction for everyone in the territory; each case judged on its merits
  │   equal_before_the_law(court)
  │   case_A: handled per due process
  │   case_B: handled per due process
  ├─ ACTUAL face   · סודי · insider (candid) ──────────────────
  │   registry("equal before the law") — OFFICIAL proclaims one uniform law; ACTUAL routes each case by its assigned status (per-case routing follows)
  │   claim[equal_before_the_law(court)] — reality: court=[case_A→military court, case_B→civilian court]  ⇒ FALSE
  │   case_A (a Palestinian resident of the occupied territory) → military court
  │   case_B (an Israeli settler in the same territory) → civilian court
  │   same act, same place — routed to different court systems by nationality, not by the law it proclaims; the military forum is the harsher one (Palestinians tried as adults at 16 vs 18 in the civilian system) [dual-court fact: sourced]
  ├─ framing (part of the spec — I8) ───────────────────────────
  │   · #G framing: the butt is THE STATE running two legal systems in one territory while proclaiming equal justice — never the people. In the occupied West Bank, Palestinians are tried in military courts and settlers in civilian courts for the same act in the same place; the military courts nominally cover everyone, but a policy routes Israeli citizens to the civilian system (nominal universality; routing by nationality). The identities are the AXIS of the documented discrimination the satire exposes and the WRONGED PARTY it defends — never the target of the joke, never the operative key (keys are cases, §9.4). Dual-court FACT: sourced (B'Tselem; UN OHCHR; Al Jazeera; Wikipedia). 'Apartheid' as a characterization of this system is a CONTESTED label — asserted by rights groups (HRW, Amnesty, B'Tselem) and rejected by Israel — flagged here, never stated as settled fact (I7). [sourced; contested]
  ├─ coalition: core=3 · still in power (no halt)
  └─ discrepancies: 1  (read-never-by-default)
